  ('Lancer',1,'Fighting Style','Choose one: Defense, Dueling (spear + shield), Great Weapon, Interception, or Two-Weapon (dual spears): while wielding a spear in each hand you add your ability modifier to the off-hand attack''s damage and draw or stow two spears at once. Swap only when you gain a level.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer',1,'Lancer Weapons and Reach','"Polearm" in Lancer features means any spear or polearm you''re proficient with. Spears have 5 ft reach; pikes, glaives, halberds, lances, and other polearms have 10 ft reach. Your reach for Lancer features is your wielded polearm''s reach.','proficiency','approved','2026-09-25',2),
  ('Lancer',1,'Dual-Wielding Spears','Spears are versatile and thrown, and count as finesse in your hands; lances are one-handed while mounted and have disadvantage against adjacent targets. You can wield a spear in each hand (each uses its one-handed die). When you take the Attack action with a one-handed spear, you can make one off-hand spear attack as a bonus action; add your ability modifier to its damage only with the Two-Weapon (dual spears) style. No shield while dual-wielding. The off-hand attack counts as a polearm attack.','feature','new',NULL,3),
  ('Lancer',1,'Polearm Stance and Reach Tactics','While wielding a polearm (your Polearm Stance), a creature entering your reach provokes an opportunity attack from you, as well as one leaving it (still uses your reaction).','feature','new',NULL,4),
  ('Lancer',2,'Brace / Skewer','Reaction when a creature you can see moves at least 10 ft toward you in a straight line and enters your reach (instead of the Reach Tactics attack): make one polearm attack. On a hit it takes +1d8 damage and its speed becomes 0 until the end of the turn. 1 use per rest (2 at 6, 3 at 13, at will from 17).','feature','new',NULL,1),
