  ('Summoner',26,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 24.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner',27,'Unbreakable Tether (2)','Unbreakable Tether: 2 uses per long rest.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner',28,'Subclass feature','Gain your subclass''s level 28 (mythic) feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner',29,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 26.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner',30,'Arch Lich','You earn the level 30 title Arch Lich.','title','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner',30,'Arch Lich Capstone','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: your summons have advantage on attack rolls and resistance to all damage; their hits against marked foes (creatures you''ve targeted with a Summoner spell since Arch Lich began) are critical hits; Lich''s Command: once per turn, Commander''s Strike lets two summons attack. The canon phylactery cheat-death is removed (one-cheat-death rule, Gabriel 2026-09-25).','feature','new',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',1,'Cantrips','Learn 2 Songsmith cantrips (3 at 4, 4 at 10).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',1,'Spellcasting','You cast Songsmith spells with CHA as a full caster, using an instrument as your focus.','feature','approved','2026-09-25',2),
  ('Songsmith',1,'Prepared Spells','Prepare CHA modifier + Songsmith level Songsmith spells after each long rest (minimum 1).','resource','new',NULL,3),
  ('Songsmith',1,'Song Spells','A song spell is any Songsmith spell you cast that has a verbal component and requires concentration. Features that name song spells (Combat Anthem, Endless Refrain, Dual Encore, Renowned Songbird) use this definition.','feature','new',NULL,4),
  ('Songsmith',1,'Song of Inspiration','Bonus action: a creature within 60 ft that can hear you gains your Inspiration die (d6; d8 at 5, d10 at 10, d12 at 15, 2d8 at 27). Within 10 minutes it can add the die to one attack roll, check, or save after seeing the roll. CHA modifier uses (minimum 1; +1 from 13) per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,5),
  ('Songsmith',2,'Jack of Measures','Add half your PB (rounded down) to ability checks you aren''t proficient in.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',2,'Song of Rest','When you and allies who can hear you spend Hit Dice in a short rest, each regains an extra 1d6 HP (1d8 at 9, 1d10 at 13, 1d12 at 17).','feature','new',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',3,'Voice','Choose Warsong, Loresong, or Diresong and gain its level 3 feature.','choice','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',3,'Expertise','Choose two skills you''re proficient in; your PB is doubled for them.','choice','canon',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',4,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 20.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',5,'Font of Inspiration','Song of Inspiration uses recharge on a short or long rest. Your die becomes d8.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',6,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 6 feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',6,'Countercharm','Action: start performing until the end of your next turn (extend by using your action each turn). You and allies within 30 ft have advantage on saves against being frightened or charmed.','feature','new',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',7,'Cunning Flourish','Once per turn, spend an Inspiration use to roll the die and add it to your AC against one attack (uses your reaction) or to one damage roll.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',8,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 20.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',9,'Spell Tier Up','You gain 5th-tier slots.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',10,'Magical Secrets-lite','Learn two spells of tiers you can cast from any class''s list (two more at 17). They count as Songsmith spells and are always prepared.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',10,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 10 feature. Your Inspiration die becomes d10.','feature','canon',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',11,'Combat Anthem','While you concentrate on a song spell, allies within 10 ft of you add +1 to attack rolls.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',12,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 20.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',13,'More Inspiration','Song of Inspiration uses = CHA modifier + 1.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',14,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 14 feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',15,'Inspiration Die d12','Your Inspiration die becomes d12.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',16,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 20.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',17,'Two More Secrets','Learn two more spells via Magical Secrets-lite (four total). You also gain 9th-tier slots.','choice','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',18,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 18 feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',19,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 22.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',20,'Maestro','You earn the level 20 title Maestro.','title','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',20,'Maestro Benefit','When you roll initiative with no Song of Inspiration uses left, you regain one.','feature','canon',NULL,2),
  ('Songsmith',21,'Endless Refrain','Once per long rest, keep a song spell running without concentration for 1 minute.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',22,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 24.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',23,'Combat Anthem Damage','Combat Anthem also adds your CHA modifier to allies'' damage once per turn.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',24,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 24 (mythic) feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',25,'Dual Encore','Action, 1 use per long rest: cast two song spells of 3rd tier or lower, spending a slot for each; if both need concentration, keep only one (Endless Refrain can hold the other).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',26,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 24.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',27,'Inspiration Die 2d8','Your Inspiration die becomes 2d8.','resource','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',28,'Voice feature','Gain your Voice''s level 28 (mythic) feature.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',29,'Ability Boost','Raise your ability scores (amount in the Shared Frame); no score can go above 26.','boost','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',30,'Renowned Songbird','You earn the level 30 title Renowned Songbird.','title','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith',30,'Renowned Songbird Capstone','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: once per turn give Song of Inspiration as a free action (still spending a use); allies within 30 ft add your CHA modifier to saves; your song spells can''t be countered by any means, including Counterweave.','feature','new',NULL,2)
) AS v(class_name, level, name, description, feature_type, source, approved_date, sort_order)
JOIN classes c ON lower(c.name) = lower(v.class_name)
ON CONFLICT (class_id, level, name) DO NOTHING;

-- ---------- subclass_features ----------
INSERT INTO subclass_features (subclass_id, level, name, description, feature_type, source, approved_date, sort_order)
SELECT s.id, v.level, v.name, v.description, v.feature_type, v.source, v.approved_date::date, v.sort_order
FROM (VALUES
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',3,'Hold the Line','Bonus action: mark a creature you can see within 30 ft for 1 minute (marking another ends the first). While it''s within 10 ft of you, the marked creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',6,'Interpose','Reaction when a creature within 5 ft of you is hit by an attack: you become the target instead and the attack uses your AC (it can still miss). PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',10,'Rally Guard','Bonus action: you and up to 3 allies within 30 ft gain temporary HP equal to 1d10 + half your Warrior level. 1 use per rest (2 at 17).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',14,'Lockdown Strike','Once per turn, when you hit the creature marked by Hold the Line, its speed becomes 0 until the start of your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',18,'Immovable','You have advantage on STR and CON saves, and you can''t be pushed, pulled, or knocked prone against your will while you''re conscious.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',24,'Zone of Denial','Ground within 15 ft of you is difficult terrain for creatures hostile to you. Once per turn you can make an opportunity attack without spending your reaction.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Vanguard',28,'Unbreakable Wall','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: allies within 10 ft of you have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage, Interpose costs no uses, and the marked creature can''t willingly leave your reach.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',3,'Weapon Bond','During a short rest, bond with up to 2 weapons you''re proficient with. You can''t be disarmed of a bonded weapon while conscious, and as a bonus action you can call one to your hand from within 60 ft.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',6,'Maneuver Dice','You gain 4 maneuver dice (d8; d10 at 14, d12 at 24), regained on a short or long rest. Learn 3 maneuvers (one more at 10, 14, and 18): Trip (target makes a STR save vs your class DC or falls prone), Disarm (STR save or drops an item), Riposte (reaction attack when a creature misses you in melee), Precision (add the die to an attack roll after seeing it), Push (STR save or pushed 15 ft), Rally (an ally gains temp HP equal to the die + STR modifier). Add the die to the attack''s damage when the maneuver hits.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',10,'Master Strike','Once per turn, when you hit with a bonded weapon, add one maneuver die to the damage without spending it (roll it; no maneuver effect).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',14,'Adaptive Form','At the start of each of your turns choose a form until your next turn: Offense (+2 damage on weapon hits), Guard (+1 AC), or Flow (+10 ft speed and your movement doesn''t provoke). Maneuver dice become d10.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',18,'Perfect Form','You gain a 5th maneuver die, and when you roll initiative with no maneuver dice left, you regain 2.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',24,'Legendary Technique','Maneuver dice become d12. Once per turn you can apply two different maneuvers to the same hit, spending a die for each.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Weaponmaster',28,'Living Weapon','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: maneuvers don''t spend dice (you still roll them), and attacks with bonded weapons score a critical hit on 18–20.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',3,'Commander''s Strike','Once per turn, when you take the Attack action, give up one attack to let an ally within 30 ft who can see or hear you use its reaction to make one weapon attack, adding a command die (d6; d8 at 10, d10 at 18, d12 at 24) to the damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',6,'Rallying Cry','Bonus action: up to 3 allies within 30 ft who can hear you regain HP equal to your Warrior level. 1 use per rest (2 at 18).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',10,'Tactical Openings','Once per turn, when you hit a creature, the next attack roll an ally makes against it before the start of your next turn has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',14,'Turn the Tide','When you roll initiative, you and allies within 30 ft gain temporary HP equal to your Warrior level. Once per long rest, as a reaction when an ally within 30 ft fails a save, it can reroll and use the new roll.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',18,'War Banner','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: plant a banner in your space. Allies within 20 ft of it add 1d4 to attack rolls and saves and can''t be frightened.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',24,'Army of One','Aura, 30 ft, always on: allies add +2 to weapon damage rolls. One Commander''s Strike can now send two allies to attack (each uses its own reaction).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Warrior','Warlord',28,'Sovereign of the Field','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: up to 4 allies within 30 ft can each use a reaction to move half their speed and make one weapon attack. For the duration, Commander''s Strike doesn''t cost you an attack.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',3,'Potent Cantrip','A creature that succeeds on a save against your damaging cantrip still takes half damage. Ward recharge: when you cast a damaging spell with a slot, your Arcane Ward regains 2 × the slot''s tier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',6,'Sculpt Spell','When you cast an area spell, choose up to 1 + the spell''s tier creatures you can see; they automatically succeed on its save and take no damage from it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',10,'Elemental Affinity','Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder. You resist that damage type and add your INT modifier to one damage roll of each spell you cast that deals it.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',14,'Empowered Evocation','Once per turn, when you roll damage for a Mage spell, reroll up to your INT modifier in damage dice and use the new rolls.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',18,'Cataclysm','1 use per long rest: when you cast an area damage spell of 5th tier or lower, double its area; creatures that fail its save are also knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',24,'Worldbreaker Beam','Action, 1 use per long rest: a 150-ft line, 10 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a DEX save, taking 20d10 force damage on a failure or half on a success; objects and structures take double.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Evoker',28,'Living Storm','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: you gain a 60 ft fly speed (hover) and resistance to lightning and your Affinity type. At the start of each of your turns, creatures you choose within 15 ft make a DEX save or take 4d10 lightning damage (half on a success). Your cantrips deal maximum damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',3,'Inscribe Arms','Gain proficiency with light armor and martial blades (shortsword, longsword, scimitar, rapier); you can cast Mage spells in light armor. Your HP maximum increases by 1 per Mage level (d6 fragility fix).','proficiency','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',3,'Runed Weapon and Runic Strike','During a long rest, inscribe one blade or staff you''re proficient with: use INT for its attack and damage rolls, and it''s your spellcasting focus. Once per turn, a hit with it deals an extra 1d6 force (2d6 at 10, 3d6 at 18, 4d6 at 24). Ward recharge: see Walking Ward.','feature','new',NULL,2),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',6,'Walking Ward','Once per turn, when you hit with your runed weapon, your Arcane Ward regains HP equal to your INT modifier. Weave Attack: when you take the Attack action with your runed weapon you attack twice, and you can replace one attack with a Mage cantrip that takes an action.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',10,'Bind Rune','Runic Strike becomes 2d6. When Runic Strike hits, brand one rune until the start of your next turn: Binding (STR save vs your spell DC or speed 0) or Sundering (the next attack roll against it has advantage).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',14,'Glyphbomb','When you hit with your runed weapon, detonate a glyph: creatures you choose within 10 ft of the target (including it) make a DEX save, taking 5d8 force on a failure or half on a success. Uses = INT modifier (min 1) per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',18,'Runic Fortress','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per rest: +2 AC, advantage on concentration saves, and a creature that hits you with a melee attack from within 5 ft takes force damage equal to your INT modifier. Runic Strike becomes 3d6.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',24,'Eternal Script','Runic Strike becomes 4d6. Weave Attack gives 3 attacks (one can still be a cantrip). Bind Rune can brand both runes on one hit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Runeweaver',28,'Name of Unmaking','1 use per long rest, on a runed-weapon hit: the target makes a CON save. On a failure it takes 10d10 force and loses one damage resistance or immunity of your choice for 1 minute; on a success, half damage only. Story-gated legends have advantage on the save.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',3,'Lorekeeper','Learn 2 skills (any) and 2 languages. You can cast any ritual spell in your book as a ritual without preparing it. Ward recharge: when you finish a short rest, your Arcane Ward regains half its capacity.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',6,'Portent Study','After each long rest roll 2d20 and record them (3 at 18). Once per turn you can replace an attack roll, save, or check by a creature you can see with one of these rolls, before the roll is made. Unused dice are lost at your next long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',10,'Spell Thief','1 use per rest: when you see a creature within 60 ft cast a spell of a tier you can cast, you learn it for 8 hours and can cast it once with your own slot. It counts as a Mage spell for you.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',14,'Mind Palace','You have advantage on INT saves, resistance to psychic damage, and your memories can''t be altered by magic without your consent. You prepare 2 extra spells.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',18,'Perfect Recall','You recall perfectly anything you saw or heard in the last month. Portent Study gives 3 dice. Once per long rest, spend 1 minute to swap all your prepared spells.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',24,'Omniscient Eye','You gain truesight to 60 ft and can''t be surprised. Once per long rest, ask the DM about one creature you can see: its resistances, immunities, vulnerabilities, and current HP are revealed truthfully.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Mage','Scholar',28,'Rewrite Reality','Action, 1 use per long rest: cast any Mage spell of 8th tier or lower without a slot or components, or undo one roll or effect from the last round (it is rerolled or never happened). Story-gated: the DM may rule a legend''s key moments can''t be rewritten.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',3,'Lingering Hex','Your Hex lasts 8 hours. When a hexed creature drops to 0 HP, you can move the Hex to a new target within range with no action.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',6,'Hex Surge','Once per turn, when you damage a hexed creature, end its Hex to deal an extra 1d8 necrotic per two Witch levels. PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',10,'Shared Misery','Once per turn, when a hexed creature takes your Hex damage, one other creature you choose within 10 ft of it takes the same bonus damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',14,'Accursed Ground','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per rest: curse a 20-ft-radius area within 60 ft. Enemies there take -2 on saves against your spells and hexes and treat it as difficult terrain.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',18,'Permanent Mark','Once per day, place a minor Hex on one creature until the next dawn. It doesn''t count toward your limit, carries the base disadvantage and one rider, and only remove-curse-level magic ends it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',20,'Hex Signature: Deepened Hex','Your Hex bonus damage becomes 3d6.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',24,'World Hex','Action, 1 use per long rest: Hex every creature you choose within 60 ft for 1 minute (they don''t count toward your limit). Hex bonus damage still applies once per turn total.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Hex Magic',28,'Name-Eater','Action, 1 use per long rest, a hexed creature within 60 ft: CHA save. On a failure, for 1 minute it can''t cast spells, has disadvantage on all d20 rolls, and loses one legendary resistance use; on a success it is incapacitated until the end of its next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',3,'Blood Price','Once per turn, when you cast a Witch spell or deal Hex damage, lose HP equal to 2 × PB (can''t be reduced) and choose: the spell''s save DC is +1, or the damage gains +2d6 necrotic.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',6,'Crimson Font','Action: lose up to your Witch level in HP; one ally within 30 ft regains twice that. PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',10,'Vampiric Hex','Once per turn, when you deal Hex bonus damage, you regain HP equal to that damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',14,'Scar Binding','Reaction when a creature within 30 ft damages you: it takes necrotic damage equal to half the damage dealt and can''t regain HP until the end of its next turn. PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',18,'Hemorrhage Ritual','New Greater Curse option, Bleeding: the target takes 3d8 necrotic at the start of each of its turns and you regain half of it (save ends).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',20,'Blood Signature: Twin Price','You can use Blood Price twice per turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',24,'Life for Power','Bonus action, 1 use per long rest: lose HP equal to 10 × a slot tier (8th tier max) to regain one expended slot of that tier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Blood Magic',28,'Red Covenant','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: Blood Price costs no HP, Vampiric Hex also heals one ally within 30 ft for the same amount, and you resist all damage from creatures you''ve hexed.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',3,'Twist Luck','Reaction when an ally within 30 ft makes an attack roll, save, or check: it rerolls and uses either result. PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',6,'Doom Dice','You have 3 doom dice (d6), regained on a short or long rest. Once per turn, after a creature you can see within 60 ft rolls a d20, spend one to add it to or subtract it from the roll.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',10,'Cut the Thread','Reaction: force a creature within 60 ft to reroll an attack roll, save, or check and use the lower result. 1 use per rest (2 at 18).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',14,'Fated Escape','Reaction when an attack would hit you: the attack misses and you teleport up to 30 ft to an unoccupied space you can see. 1 use per rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',18,'Prophetic Hex','When you place a Hex, roll a d20 and note it. Once while that Hex lasts, replace one of the target''s d20 rolls with the noted number.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',20,'Fate Signature: Heavier Dice','Doom dice become d8 and you gain a 4th die.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',24,'Rewrite Encounter','1 use per long rest, at the end of a round: choose up to 3 d20 rolls made that round; each is rerolled and the new results stand.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Fate Magic',28,'Sovereign Fate','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: doom dice become d12 and aren''t spent when used (still once per turn per creature).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',3,'Verdant Hex','Your Hex damage can be poison. While a creature is hexed, ground within 5 ft of it is difficult terrain for your enemies.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',6,'Bloom & Blight','Bonus action, choose: an ally within 30 ft regains 1d6 + CHA modifier HP, or a hexed target makes a CON save or is slowed (speed halved until the end of its next turn). CHA modifier uses per long rest.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',10,'Living Snare','1 use per rest: a hexed target is restrained (STR save ends); attacks against it have advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',14,'Canopy Veil','1 use per rest: become invisible, or gain three-quarters cover while among plants, for 1 minute. Also 1 use per rest: your party leaves no tracks for 10 minutes.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',18,'Heartwood Curse','New Greater Curse option: the target is rooted (speed 0) and takes 2d6 poison at the start of each of its turns. If it dies while cursed, a hostile bloom hexes a new enemy within 30 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',20,'Green Signature: Deep Roots','Bloom & Blight uses double and its heal becomes 2d6 + CHA modifier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',24,'Wild Coven','Aura 15 ft: allies ignore plant-based difficult terrain and enemies don''t. Your Hex damage becomes poison and ignores nonmagical resistance.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Green Magic',28,'Green Sovereign','1 use per long rest, 1 minute: use Bloom & Blight once each turn for free; hexed enemies automatically fail their first poison save.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',3,'Witch Knight Training','Gain medium armor and martial melee weapon proficiency. You do not gain shields: the Witch Knight fights with a weapon in one hand and casts with the other.','proficiency','approved','2026-09-25',1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',3,'Hex Guard','You have +2 AC against a creature you''ve hexed, and medium armor doesn''t hinder your spellcasting.','feature','canon',NULL,2),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',6,'Cursed Strike','Once per turn, when you hit a hexed target with a melee attack, choose: its speed drops by 10 ft until the start of your next turn, or it has disadvantage on its next attack.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',6,'Extra Attack (2)','When you take the Attack action with a melee weapon, you make 2 attacks.','feature','new',NULL,2),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',10,'Black Plate','You resist necrotic and psychic damage from creatures you''ve hexed. When a hexed creature hits you, you can spend an Evil Eye use as a reaction against it.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',14,'Dread Charge','Bonus action: Dash toward a hexed target. Your next melee attack against it this turn has advantage and adds your CHA modifier to damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',18,'Hexblade Ascendant','Bond two weapons; both count as your focus. You can deliver Greater Curse through a melee hit (the target saves as normal) instead of using an action.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',20,'Knight Signature: Spellblade','You can replace one attack of your Attack action with a Witch cantrip.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',24,'Living Hexplate','Allies within 10 ft of you share your Hex Guard bonus.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Witch','Witch Knight',28,'Warlock of the Field','1 use per long rest, 1 minute: every melee hit you land applies your Hex to the target.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',3,'Verdant Bind','Channel Divinity, action: one creature within 30 ft makes a STR save or is restrained for 1 minute (save ends), and one ally within 30 ft gains 5 + Paladin level temporary HP. Oath spells: Warm Hands, Grasping Vines (3rd tier at 9: Second Breath, Overgrowth).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',7,'Aura of Living Root','You and allies in your aura resist poison damage, reduce necrotic damage taken by your CHA modifier, and have advantage on saves against being moved or knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',15,'Life-Smite','Once per turn, when you use Divine Smite, you or an ally in your aura regains HP equal to half the smite''s extra damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',18,'Ochre''s Endurance','When you drop to 0 HP and aren''t killed outright, you drop to 1 HP instead. 1 use per long rest. The Ochre Paladin''s only cheat-death feature.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',20,'Avatar of Ochre','Your Avatar form sheds green-gold bright light 30 ft and grants a 30 ft fly speed. At the start of each of your turns you regain 10 HP (if above 0), and when you score a critical hit, you and allies in your aura regain HP equal to your CHA modifier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',24,'Mythic Canopy','Allies in your aura who start their turn with at least 1 HP regain HP equal to your CHA modifier, and they also resist necrotic damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Ochre',28,'Worldroot Ward','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: you and allies in your aura can''t be moved, knocked prone, or restrained against their will and gain temporary HP equal to your Paladin level at the start of each of their turns.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',3,'Soul Toll','Bonus action, PB uses per long rest: mark an undead, spirit, or Hollow creature within 60 ft for 1 minute. It can''t regain HP, and your weapon hits on it deal +1d6 necrotic. Oath spells: Spirit Sense, Hallowed Refuge (3rd tier at 9: Waking the Dead, Spirit Ring).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',7,'Aura of Remembrance','You and allies in your aura can''t be charmed or frightened by undead and roll death saves with advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',15,'Afterlife Smite','Your Divine Smite deals +2d8 against undead and Hollow creatures. When a smite kills a creature, its spirit truthfully answers one question you ask within the next minute.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',18,'Umbria''s Door','Action, 1 use per rest: every dying ally in your aura becomes stable and regains HP equal to your CHA modifier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',20,'Avatar of Umber','Your Avatar form wears a red-oak mantle and grants the fear aura: an enemy that starts its turn within 10 ft of you makes a WIS save or is frightened until the end of its turn. You see invisible and ethereal spirits within 60 ft, and once during the Avatar you can use Turn the Unholy / Bind the Hollow as a bonus action without spending Channel Divinity.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',24,'Mythic Requiem','Action, 1 use per long rest: each enemy of your choice within 60 ft makes a CHA save. Undead and Hollow take 10d10 radiant and are turned for 1 minute on a failure (half, not turned, on a success); other enemies take 5d10 necrotic (half on a success).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Umber',28,'Gate of Returning','10-minute ritual, 1 use per long rest, story-gated: call the willing soul of someone who died within the last 10 days. It appears for 1 hour, can speak and act with its former abilities, and can''t be forced to stay. The DM decides which souls can answer.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',3,'Veil Step','Bonus action, PB uses per long rest: you become invisible until the start of your next turn or until you attack, and your next attack roll before then has advantage. Oath spells: False Face, Prey Brand (3rd tier at 9: Terror Wave, Scryshroud).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',7,'Aura of Dread','When you hit a creature, it''s marked until the end of your next turn. While a marked enemy is in your aura, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against anyone but you.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',15,'Ambush Smite','Your Divine Smite deals +2d8 psychic when the target can''t see you or you''re hidden or invisible.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',18,'Night Judgment','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per rest: magical darkness fills a 30-ft radius around you and moves with you. You and allies in your aura can see through it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',20,'Avatar of Shadows','Your Avatar form grants a fear gaze: as a bonus action each turn, one creature within 30 ft makes a WIS save or is frightened of you until the end of its next turn. Your smites deal psychic or necrotic (your choice) and add +1d8.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',24,'Mythic Umbra','In dim light or darkness, Veil Step costs no uses and doesn''t end when you attack.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Shadows',28,'Eclipse Hunt','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: choose a creature you can see. You always know where it is, it can''t teleport or turn invisible to you, your attacks against it have advantage, and once per turn a smite against it uses maximum dice.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',3,'Star Mark','Bonus action, PB uses per long rest: outline a creature within 60 ft in starlight for 1 minute. It gains no benefit from invisibility or being hidden against you or your allies, and your attacks on it score a critical hit on 19–20 until you hit it with Divine Smite. Oath spells: Glowmark, Starlance (3rd tier at 9: Noonlight, Spellbreak).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',7,'Aura of Clarity','Your aura sheds dim starlight. You and allies in it have advantage on saves against illusions and being charmed.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',15,'Void-Edged Smite','Once per turn, the radiant damage of your Divine Smite ignores resistance, and the target makes a CON save or is knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',18,'Silent Constellation','Action, 1 use per rest: one creature within 60 ft makes a WIS save or is incapacitated for 1 minute (save ends).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',20,'Avatar of Starlight','Your Avatar form grants a 60 ft fly speed (hover). Your smite damage is split evenly between force and radiant.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',24,'Mythic Nova','Action, 1 use per long rest: enemies of your choice within 30 ft make a CON save, taking 12d10 radiant and being blinded until the end of their next turn on a failure, or half damage on a success.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Paladin','Oath of Starlight',28,'Absolute Horizon','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: every enemy in your aura is Star Marked, and you and allies in your aura have truesight to 60 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',3,'Assassinate','You have advantage on attack rolls against creatures that haven''t taken a turn yet this combat, and any hit you score against a surprised creature is a critical hit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',6,'Shadow Step','Bonus action while in dim light or darkness: teleport up to 60 ft to an unoccupied space in dim light or darkness you can see. Your next melee attack this turn has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',10,'Stalker''s Flurry','Once per turn, when you deal Sneak Attack damage on your turn, you can make one more weapon attack as a bonus action (it can''t deal Sneak Attack).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',14,'Death Strike','When you hit a surprised creature, it makes a CON save against your class DC; on a failure, the attack''s damage is doubled.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',18,'Living Shadow','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per rest: a shadow clone appears within 30 ft (your AC, 1 HP). It counts as an ally for Sneak Attack, moves 30 ft when you use a bonus action to command it, and you can Shadow Step into its space.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',24,'Mythic Umbral Twin','Living Shadow has HP equal to your Assassin level and 2 uses per rest; when you take the Attack action, the clone can make one weapon attack using your bonus (no Sneak Attack).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Shadowblade',28,'Eclipse Blade','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: darkness you can see through fills 15 ft around you, you''re invisible while in dim light or darkness, and your Sneak Attack dice become d8s.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',3,'Poisoner','After each long rest you have basic doses equal to your PB. Bonus action: coat a weapon for 1 minute or until it hits. On the hit, the target takes +2d6 poison and makes a CON save (DC 8 + PB + DEX modifier) or is poisoned until the end of its next turn.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',6,'Debilitating Mix','When a creature fails the save against your dose, also choose one: speed halved, no reactions, or disadvantage on its next attack roll (until the end of its next turn).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',10,'Toxic Blood','You resist poison damage. When a creature within 5 ft hits you with a melee attack, it takes poison damage equal to your PB.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',14,'Master Toxin','1 use per rest: one dose ignores poison resistance and immunity to the poisoned condition.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',18,'Cloudkill Kiss','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per long rest (or spend 2 doses): a 20-ft-radius toxic cloud within 60 ft, heavily obscured. A creature that enters it or starts its turn there makes a CON save, taking 6d8 poison on a failure or half on a success.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',24,'Mythic Venom Lord','You''re immune to poison damage and the poisoned condition. You have 2 × PB doses, and dose damage becomes 4d6.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Venom Bound',28,'Perfect Toxin','1 use per long rest, on a coated hit: the target makes a CON save. On a failure it drops to 0 HP; on a success it takes 10d10 poison. Story-gated legends instead take 10d10 poison and are poisoned for 1 minute.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',3,'False Face','During a short rest, craft a disguise; you have advantage on checks to pass as someone else while wearing it. You can mimic any voice you''ve heard for at least 1 minute.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',6,'Without a Trace','You leave no tracks or scent and can''t be tracked by nonmagical means. You don''t take a Stealth penalty for moving at a normal pace.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',10,'Identity Thief','Action, 1 use per rest: after studying a creature for 1 minute, take its exact appearance and voice for 1 hour. Only truesight sees through it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',14,'Vanish','1 use per rest: when you Hide in dim light or darkness, you become invisible until the end of your next turn or until you attack or cast a spell.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',18,'Ghost Walk','1 use per rest: as part of your movement, pass through one wall, door, or barrier up to 10 ft thick.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',24,'Mythic Nonperson','You can''t be targeted by divination or perceived through scrying. Creatures that aren''t hostile don''t notice you unless you interact with them.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Assassin','Ghost Walker',28,'Forgotten by the World','Action, 1 use per long rest: each non-legend creature of your choice within 30 ft makes a WIS save or forgets everything you did in the last hour; hostile ones lose track of you.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',3,'Born to the Saddle','Mounting or dismounting costs 5 ft of movement, and you have advantage on saves to stay in the saddle. While mounted, a lance has 10 ft reach, can be used one-handed, and has no disadvantage against adjacent targets. Reaction: when an attack hits your mount, it hits you instead.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',6,'Wheeling Charge','Once per turn, if you (or your mount) move at least 20 ft straight toward a creature and then hit it with a melee attack, deal +1d8 damage and it makes a STR save or falls prone. Your mount''s movement doesn''t provoke opportunity attacks from creatures you hit this turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',10,'Unseat','When you hit a mounted creature, or a Large or smaller creature with a charge, it makes a STR save or is dismounted and knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',14,'Ferocious Charger','Wheeling Charge damage becomes 2d8. When you take the Attack action while mounted, your mount can make one attack using your PB in place of its own.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',18,'Spirited Mount','1 use per rest, if you have no living mount: summon a spectral warhorse for 1 hour (AC 13 + PB, HP 5 × Knight level, speed 60 ft). It acts on your turn and obeys your commands.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',24,'Mythic Cavalry','Your mount can move through hostile creatures'' spaces. Each creature it passes through makes a DEX save or takes 2d8 bludgeoning and falls prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Cavalier',28,'Thunder of Hooves','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: allies within 30 ft gain +20 ft speed and their movement doesn''t provoke opportunity attacks. Your Wheeling Charge deals maximum damage, and creatures it hits make a WIS save or are frightened of you until the end of their next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',3,'Interpose','Reaction while wielding a shield, when an ally within 5 ft is hit: add 2 + your PB to its AC against that attack, possibly turning the hit into a miss.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',6,'Wall of Iron','While you wield a shield, at the start of each of your turns choose one ally within 5 ft; until your next turn it uses your AC if yours is higher.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',10,'Brace vs Charge','Reaction when a creature moves at least 10 ft toward you and ends within your reach: make an opportunity attack with advantage. On a hit, its speed becomes 0 until the end of its turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',14,'Phalanx Tactics','You and allies adjacent to you have half cover against ranged attacks and advantage on STR saves.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',18,'Immovable Object','You can''t be moved or knocked prone against your will, and the ground within your reach is difficult terrain for enemies.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',24,'Mythic Bastion','Unbreakable Guard works for allies within 15 ft: you move to a space adjacent to them first without provoking. Interpose adds 4 + your PB instead.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Shieldbearer',28,'Living Rampart','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: allies within 15 ft have three-quarters cover, you resist all damage, and once per turn you can use Interpose without spending your reaction.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',3,'Bodyguard''s Bond','After a short or long rest, designate one willing creature as your VIP. Reaction when a creature attacks your VIP within 10 ft of you: swap places with the VIP and become the attack''s target (it uses your AC).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',6,'Royal Challenge','When a creature attacks your VIP, you can Challenge it with no action and without spending a use.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',10,'Protector''s Strike','Reaction when a creature within your reach attacks your VIP: make one weapon attack against it first. On a hit, deal +1d8 damage and its attack has disadvantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',14,'Courtly Authority','Action, 1 use per rest: a creature within 60 ft that understands you makes a WIS save (DC 8 + PB + CHA or STR modifier) or obeys a one-word command (halt, kneel, drop, flee, approach) on its next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',18,'Die for the Crown','Unbreakable Guard costs no uses when you protect your VIP, and it works within 30 ft (you move next to the VIP first without provoking).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',24,'Mythic Regent Guard','You can have two VIPs. While within 30 ft of you, each VIP has +2 AC and resists damage from creatures you''ve Challenged.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Knight','Crown Guard',28,'Sovereign''s Shadow','1 use per long rest, reaction when a VIP within 30 ft takes damage: you take all of it instead. For the next minute you can take one extra reaction each round.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',3,'Point-Blank or Longshot','Choose permanently. Point-Blank: no disadvantage on ranged attacks for being within 5 ft of an enemy. Longshot: your ranged weapons'' normal and long ranges increase by half, and you ignore half cover at long range.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',6,'Aimed Shot','Bonus action: your next ranged weapon attack this turn has advantage. PB uses per rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',10,'Volley','Action, 1 use per rest: make one ranged attack against each creature you choose within a 10-ft radius of a point in range (one ammunition each).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',14,'Piercing Round','1 use per rest: when you hit with a ranged attack, the shot continues to a second creature in a straight line behind the first; roll a separate attack against it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',18,'Rain of Arrows','Bonus action, 1 use per rest: make three ranged weapon attacks against marked or favored enemies.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',24,'Mythic Bowman','1 use per rest: a ranged attack ignores full cover if you know the target''s location (the shot curves or punches through).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Archer',28,'Horizon Kill','1 use per long rest: a ranged hit against your marked quarry in sight is automatically a critical hit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',3,'Companion','Bond a beast companion (land, air, or water form). Medium, AC 13 + PB, HP 5 + 5 × Ranger level, speed 40 ft (air: fly 60 ft, HP 4 × Ranger level + 4), your saves. Attack: + PB + WIS modifier to hit, 1d8 + PB damage. It acts on your initiative right after you and Dodges unless you spend a bonus action to command it (or replace one of your attacks with its attack). If it dies, bond a new one after a long rest.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',6,'Coordinated Attack','Once per turn, when you hit a creature, your companion can use its reaction to attack that creature.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',10,'Beast''s Defense','Your companion gains Evasion. 1 use per rest, it can also halve one attack''s damage as a reaction.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',14,'Shared Mark','Your companion''s hits deal your Hunter''s Mark damage (once per turn) against your marked target.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',18,'Primal Bond','Your companion resists nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage, and makes death saves instead of dying at 0 HP.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',24,'Mythic Alpha','Choose: a second, lesser companion (half HP, no Shared Mark), or your companion grows Large (HP doubled, damage 2d8 + PB).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Tamer',28,'Twin Souls','Once on each of your turns, your companion makes one attack for free without your command, and you and your companion share Hunter''s Mark concentration (damage to either can''t break it).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',3,'Twin Blades and Hexed Steel','Two-weapon fighting is built in: you add your ability modifier to off-hand damage, and the off-hand weapon needn''t be light if both are finesse. You learn one extra Ranger cantrip and gain expanded spells: choose one illusion or movement Mage spell of a tier you can cast now and at 5, 9, and 13; they count as Ranger spells and are always prepared; your spell DC can use DEX or WIS.','proficiency','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',6,'Skirmish Spell','1 use per rest: after you hit with both weapons on your turn, cast a 1st-tier Ranger spell as a bonus action.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',10,'Flurry Mark','When both of your weapons hit the same creature in one turn, apply or refresh Hunter''s Mark on it without an action or a free cast.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',14,'Blurred Steps','After you Disengage or cast a movement spell, your next dual-wield attack before the end of your next turn has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',18,'Spellsteel','When you hit with a melee weapon, spend a slot: +2d8 force for a 1st-tier slot, +1d8 per tier above 1st (max 5d8). Once per turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',24,'Mythic Stalker','1 use per long rest: concentrate on two Ranger spells at once for 1 minute.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Ranger','Stalker',28,'Twin Weave Blades','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: each Attack action is five finesse strikes (canon said four; raised by one because the Ranger now has 4 attacks at 20); you can replace one with a Ranger cantrip.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',3,'Bark Ward','At the start of your turn, if you''re touching natural wood, earth, or stone, you gain temporary HP equal to your PB + WIS modifier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',6,'Land''s Grasp','Once per turn, when a Druid spell hits a creature or it fails a save against one, it also makes a STR save or is restrained until the end of its next turn. WIS modifier uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',10,'Tree Stride','1 use per rest: using 5 ft of movement, step into a tree and out of another you know within 500 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',14,'Anchor Echo','Once per long rest, commune with an anchor-bound site within 1 mile and ask the DM three questions about it. While touching the ground you have tremorsense to 30 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',18,'Living Grove','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: a 30-ft-radius grove within 60 ft. Allies starting their turn in it regain WIS modifier HP; it''s difficult terrain for enemies, and an enemy entering it for the first time on a turn makes a STR save or is restrained (save ends).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',24,'Mythic Worldtree','Bark Ward temporary HP doubles. Living Grove has a 60-ft radius and 2 uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Roots',28,'Root of Ages','Action, 1 use per long rest: roots erupt within 60 ft of you. Enemies there make a STR save, taking 10d8 bludgeoning and being restrained for 1 minute on a failure (save ends), or half damage on a success.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',3,'Combat Shape','You can Wild Shape as a bonus action, and your CR limit is your Druid level ÷ 3 (minimum 1) if higher than the table. While shaped, bonus action: spend a slot to regain 1d8 HP per slot tier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',6,'Primal Strike','Your beast attacks count as magical, and once per turn a beast hit deals +1d8 force.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',10,'Elemental Shape','Spend two Wild Shape uses to become an air, earth, fire, or water elemental of CR up to your limit + 1.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',14,'Hybrid Form','Bonus action, no use spent: keep your own body and statistics but gain natural weapons (magical, 1d10 + WIS modifier, WIS to hit), +2 AC, and one beast movement mode (climb, swim, or 30 ft fly) for 10 minutes.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',18,'Apex Predator','While shaped, your first hit each turn deals +2d8, and you have advantage on attacks against creatures below half HP. When you shift, creatures you choose within 30 ft make a WIS save or are frightened of you for 1 minute (save ends). (Circle of Beasts keeps this name; the Berserker''s L30 title is Wrathborn.)','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',24,'Mythic Chimera Shape','When you shift, combine the traits of up to three beasts you''ve seen: all their movement modes and senses, and one special attack from each.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Beasts',28,'Thousand Forms','Once per turn, as part of your movement, shift into another form without spending a use. Your form pool becomes 4 × Druid level.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',3,'Seasonal Boon','After each long rest choose a season. Spring: your healing spells restore +WIS modifier HP. Summer: once per spell, add WIS modifier to fire or radiant damage. Autumn: a creature that fails your spell''s save has -1d4 on its next save. Winter: creatures you deal cold damage to lose 10 ft of speed until your next turn.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',6,'Weather Call','Action, concentration up to 10 minutes, 1 use per rest: within 60 ft of you call rain (lightly obscured, extinguishes flames), gale (ranged weapon attacks have disadvantage), fog (heavily obscured), or heat (allies resist cold).','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',10,'Sudden Season','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per rest: flip a 30-ft-radius zone within 60 ft. Spring: allies starting their turn there regain 1d6 HP. Summer: enemies starting there take 2d6 fire. Autumn: enemies there have disadvantage on WIS saves. Winter: difficult terrain, and enemies starting there take 2d6 cold.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',14,'Storm Shape','As a Wild Shape option, become a living storm: fly 60 ft (hover), resist lightning and thunder, and creatures you choose that start their turn within 10 ft make a DEX save or take 2d8 lightning.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',18,'Year''s Cycle','You hold two Seasonal Boons at once, and you can change them on a short rest.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',24,'Mythic Equinox','You hold all four Seasonal Boons. Sudden Season has a 60-ft radius and 2 uses per rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Druid','Circle of Seasons',28,'Eternal Season','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: a 120-ft radius around you becomes the season of your choice, applying Sudden Season effects with doubled dice.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',3,'Frenzy','When you rage, you can choose to frenzy: for that rage you can make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action on each of your turns. When the rage ends, you gain 1 level of exhaustion.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',6,'Mindless Rage','While raging, you''re immune to being charmed or frightened; such effects on you end when you enter a rage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',10,'Retaliation','Reaction when a creature within 5 ft damages you: make one melee weapon attack against it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',14,'Improved Frenzy','Your first frenzy each long rest causes no exhaustion, and a short rest removes one level of exhaustion gained from frenzy.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',18,'Relentless Assault','Once per turn, when you drop a creature to 0 HP with a melee attack, move up to 10 ft (no opportunity attacks) and make one more melee weapon attack.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',24,'Mythic Blur of Blades','Your frenzy bonus action makes two melee weapon attacks instead of one.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Frenzy',28,'Storm of Slaughter','Action while raging, 1 use per long rest: move up to your speed without provoking, and make one melee weapon attack against each creature that comes within your reach during the move.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',3,'Thick Skin','While raging, you gain +1 AC (stacks with Unarmored Defense or armor).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',6,'Guarded Stance','Reaction while raging, when you''re hit: reduce the damage by 1d10 + CON modifier. PB uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',10,'Bastion Rage','1 use per rest, when you enter a rage: for that rage, allies adjacent to you reduce bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage they take by your CON modifier.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',14,'Immovable','While raging, you can''t be moved or knocked prone against your will, and you have advantage on saves and checks against being grappled or restrained.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',18,'Juggernaut','While raging, difficult terrain doesn''t slow you, and you can move through the space of a Large or smaller hostile creature; it makes a STR save or falls prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',24,'Mythic Iron Body','While raging, critical hits against you become normal hits, and Thick Skin becomes +3 AC.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Ironhide',28,'Unbreakable Mountain','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: reduce all damage you take by your CON modifier + PB, and allies adjacent to you resist bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',3,'Blood Fracas','While you''re at or below half your HP (bloodied), once per turn your melee hits deal +1d6.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',6,'Crimson Feed','Once per turn, when you score a critical hit or drop a creature to 0 HP with a melee attack, regain 1d10 + CON modifier HP.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',10,'Scent of Blood','You know the location of any bloodied creature within 60 ft that isn''t behind total cover, and you have advantage on checks to track bloodied creatures.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',14,'Hemorrhage','Once per turn, when you hit while raging, the target bleeds: it takes 1d6 slashing at the start of each of its turns for 1 minute (CON save at the end of each of its turns ends it; doesn''t stack).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',18,'Blood Storm','Bonus action while raging, 1 use per rest: enemies within 10 ft make a CON save, taking 4d8 necrotic and starting to bleed (as Hemorrhage) on a failure, or half damage on a success. You regain HP equal to half the total damage dealt.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',24,'Mythic Red Tide','While raging, Blood Fracas applies even when you aren''t bloodied, and its die becomes a d10.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Berserker','Bloodwake',28,'Carnage Sovereign','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: your melee attacks score a critical hit on 18–20 against bloodied creatures, and Crimson Feed has no once-per-turn limit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',3,'Tiger''s Rush','Your speed increases by 10 ft. If you move at least 20 ft on your turn before your first unarmed strike, that strike has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',6,'Pounce','Once per turn, when the Tiger''s Rush strike hits, the target makes a STR save or falls prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',10,'Raking Flurry','Each Flurry strike that hits deals an extra 1d4 slashing damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',14,'Predator''s Eye','Bonus action, 1 Focus: mark a creature for 1 minute. You know where it is within 60 ft, and your first strike against it each turn has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',18,'Hunting Rhythm','When you hit the same creature with three or more strikes in one turn, the last one deals +2d8 and the creature can''t take reactions until the start of your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',24,'Mythic Tiger','Your speed increases by another 20 ft, Tiger''s Rush needs only 10 ft of movement, and you can move after striking without provoking from the creature you struck.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Tiger',28,'Sovereign Cat','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: the Tiger''s Rush advantage applies to all your strikes, and once per turn a hit on a prone creature deals +2d8.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',3,'Crushing Grab','Once per turn, when you hit with an unarmed strike, you can also try to grapple the target (Large or smaller; STR or DEX save vs your class DC). You can still Flurry while grappling.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',6,'Thick Hide','You gain +1 AC, and at the start of each of your turns while you''re grappling a creature you gain temporary HP equal to your PB.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',10,'Maul','Your strikes against a creature you''re grappling deal +1d8.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',14,'Unbearable Hold','A creature you grapple has disadvantage on attacks against anyone but you and on checks or saves to escape, and it can''t teleport.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',18,'Hibernating Guard','Bonus action, 1 use per rest: gain temporary HP equal to twice your Pugilist level and advantage on CON saves for 1 minute.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',24,'Mythic Bear','You can grapple two creatures at once and grapple Huge creatures. Maul becomes 2d8.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of the Bear',28,'Mountain''s Hug','Action, 1 use per long rest: a creature you''re grappling makes a CON save, taking 10d10 bludgeoning and being stunned until the end of your next turn on a failure, or half damage on a success.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',3,'Iron Bones','While unarmored, you gain +1 AC.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',6,'Break Guard','1 use per rest: when you hit, the target''s AC drops by 2 until the end of your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',10,'Shockwave Palm','When you hit, spend 1 Focus: the target makes a STR save or is pushed 15 ft and knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',14,'Shatterplate','1 use per rest: when you hit, the target''s armor stops counting until the end of your next turn (its AC becomes 10 + DEX modifier + shield or natural bonus).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',18,'Siege Fists','Your strikes deal double damage to objects and structures and +1d8 to constructs.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',24,'Mythic Iron','Iron Bones becomes +3 AC. Break Guard can be used once per turn by spending 1 Focus.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Pugilist','Way of Iron',28,'Living Anvil','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: you can''t be moved or knocked prone, and each of your hits lowers the target''s AC by 1 (max -5) until the effect ends.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',3,'Lockstep','While an ally within 5 ft of you wields a polearm or reach weapon, you and that ally gain +1 AC.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',6,'Wall of Points','Allies within 5 ft of you have half cover against attacks from creatures that are closer to you than to them.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',10,'Hold Fast','You and allies within 10 ft of you have advantage on saves and checks against being shoved, pushed, or knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',14,'Combined Brace','When you use Brace / Skewer, one ally within 10 ft wielding a melee weapon can use its reaction to attack the same creature.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',18,'Fortress Line','Allies within 10 ft of you who wield polearms gain your Reach Tactics benefit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',24,'Mythic Phalanx','Lockstep becomes +2 AC, and Wall of Points grants three-quarters cover.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Phalanx',28,'Unbroken Spearwall','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: you and allies within 15 ft can''t be moved or knocked prone, and each of them can make one opportunity attack per round without spending a reaction.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',3,'Vault Strike','Your standing jumps cover the distance of running jumps. Once per turn, if you jump at least 10 ft right before a melee attack, it deals +1d8.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',6,'Leaping Charge','Your jump distance doubles, and your jumps don''t provoke opportunity attacks.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',10,'Aerial Threat','1 use per rest: after you jump or while you''re above your target, you have advantage on all your attacks this turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',14,'Dragoon Descent','Action, 1 use per rest: leap up to 60 ft and land in a space you can see, taking no falling damage. Creatures within 5 ft of where you land make a DEX save, taking 4d10 piercing and falling prone on a failure, or half damage on a success.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',18,'Skyhook','Bonus action: hook a surface or creature within your reach + 10 ft and pull yourself next to it. When you hit a flying creature, it makes a STR save or is dragged down to the ground within your reach and knocked prone.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',24,'Mythic Vault','On your turn you have a 30 ft fly speed as long as you end your move on a surface. Dragoon Descent has 2 uses per rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Skyreach',28,'Starfall Lance','1 use per long rest, replacing a Dragoon Descent: leap up to 120 ft; creatures within 20 ft of where you land make a DEX save, taking 10d10 force and falling prone on a failure, or half on a success. Then make one polearm attack against each creature within your reach.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',3,'Twin Fangs','While wielding a spear in each hand you gain the Two-Weapon (dual spears) style benefits (if you already have it, swap it for another Lancer style). Once per turn, when both spears hit the same creature on your turn, Measured Thrust slows it by 20 ft instead of 10.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',6,'Crossed Guard','While wielding a spear in each hand you gain +1 AC. From level 7, your Haft Parry bonus also applies to every other attack the same creature makes against you that turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',10,'Double Brace','While dual-wielding, Brace / Skewer attacks with both spears (two rolls). The +1d8 applies to one hit of your choice; the stop applies if either hits.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',14,'Flurry of Points','Your off-hand bonus action makes two attacks with the off-hand spear instead of one.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',18,'Paired Sentinel','Once per round, when you make an opportunity attack while dual-wielding, attack with each spear as part of the same reaction.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',24,'Mythic Twinstrike','Once per turn, when you hit a creature with one spear after hitting it with the other earlier that turn, the second hit is a critical hit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Lancer','Twinstrike',28,'Two Spear Tempest','Action, 1 use per rest: move up to your speed without provoking. Make one attack with each spear against each creature that comes within your reach during the move (max one per spear per creature); Measured Thrust can apply to each creature hit.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',3,'Radiant Flood','Channel Divinity, action: enemies of your choice within 30 ft make a CON save, taking 2d10 + Priest level radiant on a failure or half on a success (undead and Hollow have disadvantage).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',6,'Coronal Ward','Reaction when an ally within 30 ft takes damage: reduce it by 2d6 + WIS modifier. WIS modifier uses per long rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',10,'Dawnfire','Once per turn, when your Priest cantrip or spell deals damage, add your WIS modifier as radiant damage; a creature hit sheds dim light and can''t benefit from being invisible until your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',14,'Mass Disciple','One use of Disciple''s Touch can heal up to 3 creatures within range.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',18,'Sun Mantle','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per rest: you shed bright light 30 ft, resist radiant and necrotic damage, and enemies that start their turn within 10 ft of you take radiant damage equal to WIS modifier + PB.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',24,'Mythic Halo','Sun Mantle has unlimited uses, and allies within its light resist necrotic damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Lightbearer',28,'Day Without Night','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: true sunlight fills 120 ft around you and dispels magical darkness of 8th tier or lower. Enemies in it have disadvantage on attack rolls, allies starting their turn in it regain WIS modifier HP, and undead and Hollow starting there take 4d10 radiant.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',3,'Seal','Bonus action, PB uses per long rest: a spirit, undead, fiend, or Hollow within 60 ft makes a CHA save or is restrained for 1 minute (save ends).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',6,'Abjure','Reaction, 1 use per rest: when you or an ally within 30 ft would be possessed, charmed, or frightened, the effect fails.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',10,'Circle of Binding','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per rest: a 15-ft-radius circle within 60 ft. Undead, fiends, spirits, and Hollow can''t willingly enter or leave it, and those inside have disadvantage on attack rolls.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',14,'Hollow-Breaker','Your damage against undead and Hollow ignores resistance, and your Destroy threshold is 2 higher against Hollow.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',18,'Soul Lock','Action, 1 use per long rest: a creature within 60 ft makes a CHA save or can''t teleport, change planes, or turn ethereal for 1 minute. A sealed creature that dies within that minute can''t be raised or reanimated.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',24,'Mythic Sigil','Seal works on any creature type and can target two creatures per use.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Binder',28,'Absolute Seal','Action, 1 use per long rest: a creature within 60 ft makes a CHA save. On a failure it''s incapacitated and restrained for 1 minute with no repeat save; on a success it''s restrained until the end of its next turn. Legends can spend a legendary resistance as normal.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',3,'Whisper in the Dark','Bonus action: send a whisper only one creature within 60 ft can hear (it can reply the same way). Once per rest, touching a creature dead less than 1 minute, you hear its last thoughts.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',6,'Umbra Sight','You see normally in magical and nonmagical darkness to 60 ft, and you know when a creature you can see within 30 ft tells a deliberate lie.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',10,'Secret Debt','1 use per rest: a creature that heard your whisper within the last hour makes a WIS save or must answer one question truthfully.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',14,'Shadow Step, Sacred','Bonus action in dim light or darkness: teleport up to 30 ft to a dim or dark space you can see. Allies within 5 ft of where you arrive have half cover until your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',18,'Congregation of Whispers','You and allies within 120 ft can speak telepathically, and they have advantage on saves against being charmed.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',24,'Mythic Umbra Choir','Bonus action, PB uses per long rest: up to WIS modifier creatures within 60 ft hear dreadful whispers; each makes a WIS save or takes 4d8 psychic and is frightened until the end of its next turn (half, not frightened, on a success).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Priest','Shadow Whisper',28,'Night''s Confessor','1 use per long rest: compel the full truth from a willing or defeated foe.','feature','canon',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',3,'Bone Servant','Your lesser template becomes Bone Servant: Medium undead, speed 30 ft (no fly), immune to poison damage and the poisoned, exhaustion, and charmed conditions, Rusted Blade deals slashing or piercing; doesn''t need air, food, or sleep. From 5, your greater template is Grave Guard: Medium undead, reach 5 ft, same immunities, Grave Blade deals necrotic and a creature it hits can''t regain HP until the start of your next turn.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',6,'Grave Command','Action, 1 use per rest: an undead within 30 ft with CR no higher than half your Summoner level makes a WIS save or obeys you for 1 minute (it doesn''t use capacity).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',10,'Soul Relay','1 use per rest: when a creature dies within 30 ft of one of your summons, you regain PB + CHA modifier HP and can raise it as an extra Bone Servant for 1 minute outside your capacity.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',14,'Remnant Army','Action, 1 use per rest: raise up to CHA modifier corpses within 30 ft as Bone Servants at half HP for 1 minute, outside your capacity.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',18,'Death Knight Guard','Your Grave Guard gains +2 AC, makes two Grave Blade attacks per Attack action, and can use its reaction to impose disadvantage on an attack against you from within 5 ft of it.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',24,'Mythic Ossuary','Your Bone Servants take half damage from area effects. Remnant Army has 2 uses per rest and raises servants at full HP.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Necromancer',28,'Door of the Dead','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: open a door within 30 ft. At the start of each of your turns a full-HP Bone Servant steps out (outside capacity, max 5). Creatures that start their turn within 10 ft of the door make a CON save or take 4d10 necrotic.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',3,'Hollow Spark','Your summons are Hollow (a creature type: mana-drained husks; features that affect undead also affect Hollow). Lesser template Hollow Husk: Medium, speed 30 ft, climb 30 ft (no fly), resists necrotic, Clutching Rot deals necrotic; Hunger: once per turn +PB damage to a creature below half HP. From 5, greater template Hollow Brute: Large, speed 30 ft, climb 20 ft, reach 10 ft, resists necrotic, Rending Swipe deals bludgeoning and gives the target disadvantage on its next CON save. Spark: when your Hollow summon hits a concentrating creature, it has disadvantage on that concentration save.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',6,'Shared Hunger','Once per turn, when a Hollow summon deals Hunger damage, you regain HP equal to that damage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',10,'Rot Mark','Bonus action: mark a creature within 60 ft for 1 minute. Your summons have advantage on attacks against it, and it can''t regain HP above half its maximum.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',14,'Hollow Pack','Your binding capacity is 1 point higher, but the extra point can only hold a Hollow Husk.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',18,'Break the Seal','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest, story-gated: your summons gain +PB damage and advantage on attacks. When it ends, roll a d6 per summon; on a 1 that summon breaks free and becomes hostile until it''s destroyed or rebound. The DM may rule that breaking the seal draws attention.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',24,'Mythic Rot Choir','Enemies that start their turn within 10 ft of any of your Hollow summons take necrotic damage equal to your PB and have disadvantage on concentration saves until their next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Hollowmancer',28,'Spell Rot Sovereign','Reaction, 1 use per long rest: when you see a creature within 60 ft cast a spell, it makes a CHA save vs your spell DC. On a failure the spell fails and you regain an expended slot of its tier (6th max).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',3,'Scrap Drone','Your lesser template becomes Scrap Drone: Small construct, fly 30 ft (hover), walk 10 ft, immune to poison and psychic damage and the poisoned, charmed, and exhaustion conditions; Bolt Launcher is a ranged spell attack (60 ft, piercing); during a short rest you can restore all its HP without rebinding. From 5, your greater template is Iron Sentinel: Medium construct, AC 15 + PB, speed 25 ft, reach 5 ft, same immunities, Piston Fist deals bludgeoning; Guard Protocol: reaction to impose disadvantage on an attack against you from a creature within 5 ft of it.','resource','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',6,'Overclock','Bonus action, 1 use per rest: one construct summon gets +10 ft speed and one extra strike each turn for 1 minute; when it ends, the construct takes force damage equal to 2 × your PB.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',10,'Iron Phalanx','Your constructs gain +1 AC while within 5 ft of another of your constructs, and you gain +1 AC while within 5 ft of one.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',14,'Siege Frame','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: merge your constructs into one Large Siege Frame (AC 16 + PB, HP equal to their combined current HP, two strikes of 3d10 + PB bludgeoning, double damage to objects and structures). When it ends, they separate with the HP left split evenly.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',18,'Black Gate Echo','Action, 1 use per long rest: bind an extra Iron Sentinel for 1 minute outside your capacity.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',24,'Mythic Assembly','You can rebind a destroyed construct as a bonus action once per turn (it returns at half HP), and Field Repair works on all your constructs as an action once per rest.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Summoner','Technomancer',28,'Voice Beyond the Gate','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: each of your constructs can take one extra action on each of its turns (Attack or Dodge only).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',3,'Battle Chorus','Gain medium armor and martial weapon proficiency. A creature holding your Inspiration die can add it to one weapon damage roll, or to its AC against one attack (reaction).','proficiency','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',6,'Fear Breaker','Starting Countercharm ends the frightened condition on allies within 30 ft, and while you perform they''re immune to being frightened.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',10,'War Cadence','You make 2 attacks when you take the Attack action, and you can replace one of them with a Songsmith cantrip.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',14,'Thunder Refrain','Once per turn, when you hit with a weapon or a cantrip, deal +2d6 thunder; the target makes a STR save or is pushed 10 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',18,'March of Conquest','Bonus action, 1 use per rest: allies within 30 ft can each use a reaction to move up to half their speed without provoking, and their next attack before the end of their next turn has advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',24,'Mythic War Anthem','Combat Anthem gives +2 to attack rolls and reaches 30 ft.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Warsong',28,'Unbroken Legion','Bonus action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: allies within 30 ft are immune to being frightened or charmed and gain temporary HP equal to your Songsmith level at the start of each of their turns.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',3,'Cutting Words','Reaction when a creature within 60 ft that you can see makes an attack roll, check, or damage roll: spend an Inspiration use and subtract the die from the roll. You also gain proficiency in 3 skills of your choice.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',6,'Universal Tongue','You understand every spoken language, and any creature that knows a language understands what you say.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',10,'Peerless Skill','When you make an ability check, you can spend an Inspiration use to add the die (after seeing the roll).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',14,'Stolen Lore','Learn two more Magical Secrets-lite spells; after each long rest you can swap one of your Secrets for another.','choice','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',18,'Living Library','1 use per long rest: cast any spell of 5th tier or lower that you''ve seen cast, using one of your slots; it counts as a Songsmith spell.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',24,'Mythic Chronicle','Once per round, Cutting Words doesn''t spend a use.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Loresong',28,'Write the Room','Action, 1 use per long rest: each creature of your choice within 60 ft makes a WIS save or is enthralled for 1 minute: incapacitated and speed 0, ending if it takes damage (legends can spend a legendary resistance).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',3,'Tolling Note','Bonus action, spend an Inspiration use: a creature within 60 ft takes necrotic damage equal to the Inspiration die + CHA modifier and has disadvantage on its next save before the end of your next turn.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',6,'Requiem Ward','You and allies within 30 ft resist necrotic damage and roll death saves with advantage.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',10,'Silence Between Notes','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per rest: a 20-ft-radius sphere of silence within 60 ft. Creatures you choose are unaffected; others inside can''t hear or cast spells with verbal components.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',14,'Funeral March','While you perform Countercharm, enemies within 15 ft of you have their speed halved. Once per turn, when an enemy dies within 30 ft of you, regain an Inspiration use.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',18,'Umbria''s Echo','Action, concentration up to 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: the echo of a creature that died within 30 ft in the last minute rises beside you. Once on each of your turns it strikes a target within 30 ft (your spell attack, 2d10 + CHA necrotic).','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',24,'Mythic Lament','Once per turn, Tolling Note doesn''t spend a use, and it also hits each creature you choose within 10 ft of the target.','feature','new',NULL,1),
  ('Songsmith','Diresong',28,'Last Song','Action, 1 minute, 1 use per long rest: enemies within 60 ft make a WIS save at the start of each of their turns, taking 6d10 psychic and being frightened until the end of that turn on a failure (half, not frightened, on a success). Allies there add your Inspiration die to their first attack roll each turn.','feature','new',NULL,1)
) AS v(class_name, sub_name, level, name, description, feature_type, source, approved_date, sort_order)
JOIN cap_subclass_map mp ON mp.class_name=v.class_name AND mp.doc_name=v.sub_name JOIN classes c ON lower(c.name)=lower(mp.class_name) JOIN sub_classes s ON s.class_id=c.id AND lower(btrim(s.name))=lower(mp.db_name)
ON CONFLICT (subclass_id, level, name) DO NOTHING;

